  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (cut from upstream/main 12a6dcbf).\n\n## What changed\nThe containment kinds' hole-wall excuse (`swept::chord_dip`, read by `solid_index` under `SolidLaw::hole_walls`) used to credit every facet chord's full dip into the swept disc. That let a coarse polygon hole's flats be cut silently. It now judges each facet edge on its own:\n- **An edge with both ends on a declared rim circle** (within `RIM_TOL` = `DEV_TOL`, 0.01 mm, in XY, on an upright move) is a chord of the round wall that the region judges exactly. It keeps its whole dip.\n- **Any other edge** is credited at most `HOLE_CHORD_CREDIT` = `DEV_TOL`, 0.01 mm. That is the mesh tolerance, and the same value #1099 uses for its thread grant.\n- **Where the rims come from:** `generate::contain_into` builds them from the op's `holes` (Drill, Bore, Thread), using each hole's circle. A drill cycle also gets its own diameter at the hole centre, because a drill or tap cuts its own size there (the `tap_plate` case). They are passed through the new `verify::solid_hits_rims` and `verify::HoleRim`.\n- **Callers without rims:** `solid_hits` keeps its signature and passes no rims, so the cross-drill and probe laws get only the 0.01 mm credit. Their suites are green.\n- **The issue's case now convicts:** the octagon's corners at r 5 are on no declared rim (the thread was declared at r 4.4), so its flats are judged and the cut is a Gouge.\n\n**Why not a bare 0.01 mm cap.** That was the first commit on this branch. It false-gouged pinned round holes: `drill_op_recognizes_from_the_model_then_machines_clean` (a 16-gon r 2 that dips 0.038 mm), plus the `drill_plate` and `tap_plate` goldens (32-gons). It would have done the same on every coarse STL drilled hole.\n\n**Residual, stated in `docs/decisions/1217-chord-dip-credit.md`.** A hole declared or recognized at a polygon's own corner circle is still excused on its flats, because the declaration says it is round. Only the recognizer could tell the two apart.\n\n**Interaction with #1099 (open, #1071):** the two PRs touch different files and both use the 0.01 mm credit. This PR's constant is private and named `HOLE_CHORD_CREDIT`, so it does not collide with #1099's `verify::CHORD_CREDIT`.\n\n## Tests\n- New `crates/app/tests/hole_wall_chord.rs` (the first and third fail under the old full credit; the second passes both before and after):\n  - `a_coarse_polygon_holes_flats_cut_by_a_containment_kind_convict`: an octagon and a 16-gon (corners on r 5), cut out to r 5 by a bore orbit and a thread-mill helix with the rim declared at r 4.4 or with no rim, and by a drill with no rim. Each is a Gouge.\n  - `a_full_fidelity_round_hole_stays_clean_for_every_containment_kind`: a 96-gon hole stays clean for the drill, bore and helix, with or without its rim.\n  - `a_coarse_round_hole_is_excused_only_on_its_declared_rim`: a 32-gon at r 5 stays clean on its declared rim (drill and bore). A drill gouges when the rim is declared at r 4.4.\n- `solid_law_goldens`: its `contain_law` harness now passes the drill cycle's rims, as `contain_into` does. **No golden files changed.**\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) on the final head: **green** (sim 12 s, motion 4 s, 76 app suites 334 s).\n- Also run by hand on the final head: 32 containment-related app suites, including `golden_cl`, `solid_law`, `solid_law_goldens`, `operations`, `coarse_contain`, `drilling_cross*` and `tap_sim`. All green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The release-lane `--ignored` heavy suites.\n- The issue's Thread reproduction through the full op path (`#1071`'s `thread_mill_rim` fixture lives on #1099's branch). It is pinned at the `solid_hits_rims` seam with the same declared-r 4.4 octagon geometry.\n- Tilted (non-upright) containment moves: they read no world-XY rim and get only the capped credit. That is stricter, never looser.\n\nChangelog: The containment kinds' (drill, bore, thread) solid law no longer excuses a cut into a polygonal hole's flats: a hole-wall chord's full dip is excused only on a declared hole rim, any other at most 0.01 mm (#1217)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1217\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
